RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
April8,2013
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date beginning at
6:00 p.m.in Council Chambers.Present were: MAYOR-Richard L.Kaysen; COUNCIL MEMBERS-
Mr.Allen, Mr. Brown, Mr. Cook, Mr. Luna, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Shanor, Mr. Valdez and Ms. Williams.
Absent: Ms.Broyles.Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Lois Huff, City Treasurer, and Dan
White, City Attorney.The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Consent Agenda.(All agenda itemslisted with the designation of contained [CA) are considered
to be routine items bythe governing body and will be enacted by one motion.Therewill be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member ofthe governing body so requests and support by two other
members is received.Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be considered in its normal
Motion carried.Voting “yes”-- all members of the governing body present. Mayor Kaysen noted
Agenda Item #22(g)is being referred to Committee ofthe Whole, whichwill meet toreview theitem
on April 17at 6:00 p.m.in City Council Chambers.
[CA]Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on March 25,2013.Motion (per
Consent Agenda)carried.
Mr.Brown declared a conflict of interest (business interest in voucher payable to Ameri-Tech
HVAC Services)and vacated Council Chambers. Mr. Valdez moved to approve payment of vouchers
as presented, seconded by Mr. Allen. Motion carried. Voting“yes"-- all members of the governing
body presentin Council Chambers.Following announcement of thevote, Mr.Brown returned to
Council Chambers.
Mayor Kaysen opened a public hearing to receive comments and input for the Fiscal Year2013-
2014 Annual Action Plan, City of Cheyenne Community Development Block Grant (CDBG)
entitlement.Dean neW id auf, Housing and Community Development Office(H&CD), provided a brief
overview of the history and purpose of the CDBG program, noting the Cityhas received entitlement
grant funds since 1975.She advised the proposed plan is consistent with the 5 year Comprehensive
Consolidated Plan, and stated the anticipated allocation funding amount is $344,408.00, which is 8%
less thanlast year, and that an additional$298,086.00in recaptured and un-appropriated funds willalso
notifications and opportunities for input, and role of the Advisory Council in reviewing and
recommending projects tobefunded.She stated10 projects are proposed for funding for public service
projects, general service projects andprogram administration, and reviewed the projects and funding
amounts as recommended by the Advisory Council.Upon inquiry, Rick Parish, Director of Parks and
Recreation, provided information on the department'sfunding request for the Holliday Park ADA
accessible restroom project(facility located at 19" and Alexander) which was submitted through the
application process with the assistance ofthe City's Grants Manager.There being nofurther comments
and input, and purpose of the hearing having been met, Mayor Kaysen closed the public hearing.
